    <item>
      <title>BrainConnects 2026</title>
      <link>https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/events/brainconnects-2026/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/events/brainconnects-2026/</guid>
      <description>&lt;section style=&#34;max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/media/brainconnects/brainconnects-2026-logo.png&#34; alt=&#34;BrainConnects 2026 logo showing collaborating institutions connected by a brain network&#34; style=&#34;display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div style=&#34;width: calc(100% + 2.4rem); margin-left: -1.2rem; padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18); border-radius: 8px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fbffff 0%, #eefafa 52%, #ffffff 100%); box-sizing: border-box;&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto;&#34;&gt;
    &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase;&#34;&gt;29 September - 2 October 2026&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2 style=&#34;margin-top: 0;&#34;&gt;Watch this page for BrainConnects 2026&lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; LKCMedicine HQ, Novena Campus, NTU, Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;BrainConnects 2026 will be held from 29 September to 2 October 2026 at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. This year&#39;s meeting, themed &lt;strong&gt;Shared Signals, Connected Learning&lt;/strong&gt;, explores how learners, educators, clinicians, researchers, technologies, and environments become connected through shared neural, cognitive, physiological, and social signals. The programme brings together cognitive neuroscience, neuroimaging, learning sciences, mental health, ageing, human development, and cognitive engineering, with particular interest in hyperscanning, portable imaging, fNIRS/EEG, and multimodal approaches for studying real-world learning and interaction. We are especially excited that BrainConnects 2026 will take place alongside the NIRx and Artinis fNIRS workshop, creating opportunities for both scientific exchange and hands-on engagement with emerging neuroimaging tools. Programme details will be updated by day on the BrainConnects 2026 site; please use the Program at a Glance link below for the latest Day 1, Day 2, Day 3, and Day 4 schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1.45rem; padding-top: 1.35rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18);&#34;&gt;
      &lt;h3 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.9rem; color: #123d4a;&#34;&gt;Program at a Glance&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;div style=&#34;display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.16); border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h4 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d;&#34;&gt;Day 1&lt;/h4&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9:00-10:00 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Registration and arrival, breakfast, and poster setup&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10:00-10:30 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Opening&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10:30-11:45 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keynote 1&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11:45 am-1:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Lunch&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1:00-3:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Symposia 1: Mental Health &amp;amp; Aging&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3:30-4:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Afternoon tea and Poster Session A&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4:00-5:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Early Career Blitz 1&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.16); border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h4 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d;&#34;&gt;Day 2&lt;/h4&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9:15-10:30 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keynote 2&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10:30-11:00 am&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Morning tea&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;11:00 am-12:30 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Symposia 2: Developmental Neuroscience&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12:30-1:30 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Lunch&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1:30-3:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spotlight Symposia: fNIRS&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3:00-4:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Poster Session B and afternoon tea&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4:00-5:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Early Career Blitz 2&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5:00-6:00 pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Closing and prize ceremony&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.16); border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h4 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d;&#34;&gt;Day 3&lt;/h4&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule details to be announced&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;fNIRS workshop sessions, hands-on demonstrations, and afternoon tea. No poster session is scheduled for Day 3.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.16); border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;h4 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.65rem; color: #0f6c6d;&#34;&gt;Day 4&lt;/h4&gt;
          &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0.25rem 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule details to be announced&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Continuation of the NIRx and Artinis fNIRS workshop programme.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1.45rem; padding-top: 1.35rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18);&#34;&gt;
      &lt;h3 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.9rem; color: #123d4a;&#34;&gt;Keynote Speakers&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;div style=&#34;display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1.1rem;&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;text-align: center; padding: 0.4rem 0.65rem;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;img src=&#34;https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/media/brainconnects/benjamin-becker.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Professor Benjamin Becker&#34; style=&#34;width: 176px; height: 176px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 24%; border-radius: 50%; border: 3px solid #ffffff; box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(18, 61, 74, 0.16);&#34;&gt;
          &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 0.65rem;&#34;&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.22;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professor Benjamin Becker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.12rem; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;Department of Psychology&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.12rem; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;Director, MIND &amp;amp; AI Lab&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;The University of Hong Kong&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;text-align: center; padding: 0.4rem 0.65rem;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;img src=&#34;https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/media/brainconnects/twila-tardif.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Professor Twila Tardif&#34; style=&#34;width: 176px; height: 176px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 3px solid #ffffff; box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(18, 61, 74, 0.16);&#34;&gt;
          &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 0.65rem;&#34;&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.22;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professor Twila Tardif&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.12rem; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;Department of Paediatrics&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.12rem; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0; color: #4d6670; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.24;&#34;&gt;Senior Principal Scientist III, Translational Neurosciences, A*STAR Institute for Human Development and Potential&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div style=&#34;margin-top: 1.45rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 108, 109, 0.18);&#34;&gt;
      &lt;h3 style=&#34;margin: 0 0 0.85rem; color: #123d4a;&#34;&gt;Hosts and Workshop Partners&lt;/h3&gt;
      &lt;div style=&#34;display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 0.65rem; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; overflow-x: auto;&#34;&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex: 0 0 150px; width: 150px; height: 82px; padding: 0.2rem 0.25rem; border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
          &lt;img src=&#34;https://clinicalbrainlab.github.io/media/brainconnects/ntu-logo.png&#34; alt=&#34;Nanyang Technological University Singapore logo&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 132px; max-height: 78px; width: auto; height: auto;&#34;&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div style=&#34;display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex: 0 0 150px; width: 150px; height: 82px; padding: 0.2rem 0.25rem; border-radius: 8px; background: #ffffff;&#34;&gt;
